title: Implement multi-key statefile sink with hermetic tests
updated_at: "2026-07-23T10:46:45Z"
---
Implement c2c oc-plugin stream-write-statefiles as a sibling of the existing one-key sink. Parse independent JSONL envelopes, validate instance key before path construction, create mode-0700 instance directories, and atomically write complete state.snapshot payloads to unchanged per-instance filenames. Factor persistence narrowly without changing legacy semantics. Test two interleaved keys, repeated updates, raw c2c statefile --instance readability, unsafe/invalid keys, malformed envelopes, continuation after rejection, and old-command regression. Build target explicitly before tests via repository dune wrapper, max two threads. This is prerequisite for pi-c2c P1.M1.E2.T002.